{"type":"message","id":"1d84b1cc","parentId":"be6f39fd","timestamp":"2026-04-15T14:11:40.279Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me check the \"龙虾军团共享池\" bitable (app_token: EDGIbCsj4aooh9snuYrcSS78nLe) and the \"多AI协同知识共享池\" bitable (token: ZJ8obBGrSaO9rjsXPvhc1TdYngd) to understand the progress reporting structure.\n\nLet me also check the task update time to see if it's > 60 minutes old. The task was updated at 1775266541252 ms. Let me calculate: current time is 2026-04-15 14:11 UTC which is 2026-04-15 22:11 UTC+8. 1775266541252 ms = April 14, 2026...\n\n\nActually, I need to convert that timestamp properly. 1775266541252 ms divided by 1000 gives 1775266541 seconds. Let me work through the conversion from Unix epoch to get the actual date and time in UTC+8.\n\nFrom January 1, 2026, I can count forward: January through March gives 90 days, so by April 1 that's 1096 days total. Since April 15 is 14 days into April, the total is 1110 days from the epoch. Multiplying 1110 by 86400 seconds gives 95,904,000 seconds, which when added to the base timestamp should give me the correct UTC time.\n\nNow I'm working backwards from that total to find the remainder—subtracting the days component gives me 126,841 seconds, which converts to about 35 hours and 14 minutes. So the task was last updated around 35 hours and 14 minutes ago from the current time.\n\nThat means it's definitely stale (well over 60 minutes), but I should double-check whether this recurring weekly task is actually meant to be updated right now or if it's supposed to run at a different time.\n\nLooking at the task metadata more carefully: it was created on April 10, 2026 and last updated around April 14, which aligns with it being a Friday recurrence. The issue is that the due date timestamp seems to be in the future (around May 1, 2026), which doesn't match what I'd expect for a weekly Friday task. I need to figure out what the actual due date should be and whether the task is actually overdue or if there's a timestamp mismatch here. The timestamp 1775368800000 converts to Friday, May 1, 2026 at midnight UTC+8, which aligns with the weekly Friday recurrence pattern. Since today is Wednesday, April 15, the task isn't overdue yet—it's actually due in about two weeks. Now I need to check the bitable to see how work progress should be reported."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_1ndxqi319d1x_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app","arguments":{"action":"list"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776262284476,"responseId":"062ecf8ca3b19379e1263f7ee6552229"}}
